  {
    "title": "1) No learning-based data fusion",
    "subtitle": "",
    "note": "This method combines already aligned images without learning from data. At each position, it takes the normalised visible and thermal values and averages them: F = 0.5 V + 0.5 T. The single thermal channel is replicated to combine it with the three colour channels. The example of 100 and 200 averaging to 150 uses illustrative values on a common scale, not temperatures in degrees. The weights remain 50% and 50% in every region and scene, even when an input is degraded. There are no fusion weights to train. The fused image is then fed to the same YOLO detector used by the other two methods. “Non-learning-based” refers to fusion, not the detector.",
    "layout": "fixed-average",
    "elements": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "x": 0.75,
        "y": 0.9,
        "w": 11.8,
        "h": 0.85,
        "text": "1) No learning-based data fusion",
