    "note": "Fine-tuning starts from pretrained weights, not a random network. We use 100 LLVIP pairs with simulated rain on the visible input and ground truth pedestrian annotations for 3 epochs. Fusion produces an image and YOLO proposes pedestrians. The loss compares classification and location with ground truth boxes; backpropagation passes through the detector and updates only the 2,592 weights of AMG-Fuse’s final layer. The rest of the fusion network and the entire detector remain frozen. A small regularisation term limits deviation of the map from its initial version. The 20 validation pairs recommend a checkpoint; we nevertheless compare the weights actually updated after three epochs on the 50 test pairs. The common detector is prepared before the comparison and remains identical across the three methods. Validation recommends the original weights: fine-tuning is not presented as a guaranteed improvement.",
